# cm-evaluation

This repo **evaluates** frozen spatial-cognition items from
[cm-benchmark](https://github.com/andreina-covi/cm-benchmark). It does not
generate or edit items.

## Goal

Run VLMs (first: Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct) on sequential first-person frames plus
a spatial question. Compare the model output to item `answer` with
**deterministic code** (no LLM judge). Report accuracy (and later class-4
success / validity / SPL) **per construct** and per frame of reference.

## Invariants

- Consume items only (`status == ok`). Never regenerate or rewrite questions.
- System format contract lives in ``cm_benchmark.evaluation.protocol``
  (imported by `cm_evaluation.protocol`). Do not copy it here or bake it
  into item JSON. Install cm-benchmark in this env; use
  `pip install -e /path/to/cm-benchmark` so local protocol edits apply
  immediately.
- Classes 1–3: MCQ letter match. Class 4: action sequence; skip metric
  scoring until the nav graph is wired — do not fake a letter score.
- **No hardcoded machine paths.** Roots are CLI arguments (`--data-root`,
  `--items`, `--frames-root`, `--images`), like cm-benchmark. Pin `HF_HOME`
  under `--data-root` before importing `transformers`. Do not copy episode
  frames; resolve them via `--frames-root`.

## First model

`Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct`: multi-image chat, `do_sample=False`, resume-safe
JSONL predictions. More model runners later, same item/scoring pipeline.
